WEBVTT

00:00:07.860 --> 00:00:10.820
<b>Nagaoka Fireworks Festival: 
August 2-3, 2016</b>

00:00:10.820 --> 00:00:13.030
<b>Misudachi Fireworks Company</b>

00:00:13.030 --> 00:00:15.110
<b>Nagaoka Misudachi</b>

00:00:43.470 --> 00:00:44.560
All right!

00:00:44.860 --> 00:00:46.530
On with the usual!

00:00:47.480 --> 00:00:49.060
An evacuation advisory has been issued.

00:00:49.690 --> 00:00:51.260
The rainfall over the past 24 hours

00:00:51.260 --> 00:00:54.530
has exceeded what's typically expected 
over the entire month this time of year.

00:00:54.940 --> 00:00:58.630
Tanizaki City should remain on alert for 
mudslides due to rain saturating the soil.

00:00:59.630 --> 00:01:03.790
Next up is news on the continued problems 
related to the CROWDS phenomenon...

00:01:04.870 --> 00:01:08.540
<b>Nationwide Damage from Red CROWDS Activity
 Convenience Store in Saitama City</b>

00:01:05.060 --> 00:01:09.230
Yesterday saw more incidents 
by red CROWDS nationwide.

00:01:10.030 --> 00:01:12.390
Prime Minister Sugayama made a statement

00:01:11.180 --> 00:01:15.050
It sounds like the whole world's 
going to hell in a handbasket.

00:01:12.390 --> 00:01:15.270
yesterday that their origins 
are as of yet unknown—

00:01:16.680 --> 00:01:20.640
Good morning!

00:01:20.640 --> 00:01:22.640
Morning, Tsubasa.

00:01:22.640 --> 00:01:24.530
Good morning!

00:01:24.530 --> 00:01:25.430
Morning.

00:01:25.740 --> 00:01:28.400
Tsubasa, Yuru-jii is already at it.

00:01:29.920 --> 00:01:31.690
Going right over!

00:01:38.950 --> 00:01:43.000
Relax, relax, relax, relax, relax...

00:01:42.350 --> 00:01:43.400
Exhale properly!

00:01:44.100 --> 00:01:45.410
Got it!

00:01:46.960 --> 00:01:49.390
Relax, relax, relax, relax, relax...

00:01:48.150 --> 00:01:49.390
You're doing it wrong!

00:01:50.040 --> 00:01:51.500
I'm exhaling properly!

00:01:54.020 --> 00:01:55.460
This is tough!

00:01:55.460 --> 00:01:56.960
Don't complain.

00:01:56.960 --> 00:01:58.250
Okay!

00:01:59.070 --> 00:02:00.400
Hey, Yuru-jii.

00:02:00.970 --> 00:02:04.470
<b>Misudachi</b>

00:02:01.440 --> 00:02:03.740
When do I get to wear that, too?

00:02:04.180 --> 00:02:05.660
You've got a ways to go.

00:02:05.660 --> 00:02:07.590
Huh? Why?

00:02:07.590 --> 00:02:09.590
{OP}

00:03:44.370 --> 00:03:45.820
<b>UFO here</b>

00:03:52.750 --> 00:03:53.870
Don't slack.

00:03:53.870 --> 00:03:55.850
No, Yuru-jii.

00:03:55.850 --> 00:03:56.730
Look!

00:04:03.170 --> 00:04:04.240
Run!

00:04:10.050 --> 00:04:11.630
Thanks, Yuru-jii!

00:04:12.660 --> 00:04:14.230
What's this?

00:04:14.450 --> 00:04:15.640
Tsubasa!

00:04:15.640 --> 00:04:17.140
Are you okay?

00:04:17.140 --> 00:04:19.010
Oh, Kodama.

00:04:19.010 --> 00:04:20.710
Yep, I'm fine.

00:04:20.710 --> 00:04:22.920
She's okay, guys!

00:04:21.790 --> 00:04:23.090
What <i>is</i> this?!

00:04:22.920 --> 00:04:23.740
A UFO?

00:04:24.060 --> 00:04:25.290
Oh, no!

00:04:25.290 --> 00:04:28.000
And we just planted the rice!

00:04:32.730 --> 00:04:34.920
It's an alien invasion!

00:04:35.180 --> 00:04:37.610
Come save us, Gatchaman!

00:04:39.440 --> 00:04:40.840
<b>Ichinose Hajime 
 Incoming Call</b>

00:04:41.150 --> 00:04:42.940
"Ichinose Hajime"...?

00:04:42.940 --> 00:04:44.590
<i>The</i> Ichinose Hajime?

00:04:44.890 --> 00:04:46.290
It's Hajime-chan!

00:04:52.240 --> 00:04:53.680
Nice to meet you!

00:04:53.680 --> 00:04:55.940
I'm Ichinose Hajime, a Gatchaman!

00:04:57.540 --> 00:04:58.530
I'm Tsubasa!

00:04:58.530 --> 00:04:59.670
Nice to meet you!

00:04:59.670 --> 00:05:01.900
Everything's going to be 
okay now, Tsubasa-chan!

00:05:02.200 --> 00:05:04.740
I'm so happy we met!

00:05:04.740 --> 00:05:05.800
Nice to meet you!

00:05:05.800 --> 00:05:06.850
Nice to meet you!

00:05:06.850 --> 00:05:07.990
Oh, it's Paiman!

00:05:07.990 --> 00:05:09.460
Utsutsu-chan!

00:05:09.460 --> 00:05:12.520
We've come here to Nagaoka 
City in Niigata Prefecture

00:05:12.520 --> 00:05:14.810
to place an extraterrestrial 
life form under our protection!

00:05:14.810 --> 00:05:17.080
This is so cute!

00:05:17.080 --> 00:05:18.080
Oh...

00:05:20.230 --> 00:05:22.000
Oh, is that your grandpa?

00:05:22.320 --> 00:05:23.900
He's my great-grandfather.

00:05:23.900 --> 00:05:24.980
I'm Hajime!

00:05:24.980 --> 00:05:26.620
Nice to meet you!

00:05:26.980 --> 00:05:28.840
Hello, Hajime-chan.

00:05:32.160 --> 00:05:34.520
Hajime-chan, this way, please!

00:05:35.150 --> 00:05:36.430
I'm gloomy...

00:05:36.430 --> 00:05:37.770
Good luck, Gatchaman!

00:05:38.050 --> 00:05:39.290
A UFO and the Gatchaman!

00:05:38.670 --> 00:05:40.300
Mom!

00:05:39.290 --> 00:05:41.090
Nagaoka City might become super famous!

00:05:40.300 --> 00:05:41.770
My sock!

00:05:42.060 --> 00:05:44.470
Okay, everyone! Stand back!

00:05:44.470 --> 00:05:45.500
UFO!

00:05:45.500 --> 00:05:47.290
I told you to stand back!

00:05:47.290 --> 00:05:49.410
The alien might be dangerous!

00:05:50.190 --> 00:05:51.660
Hajime, stay on guard!

00:05:52.140 --> 00:05:53.160
Roger!

00:05:53.500 --> 00:05:55.730
Go, Bird!

00:05:59.430 --> 00:06:01.090
She transformed!

00:06:01.390 --> 00:06:03.050
Alien-san!

00:06:03.050 --> 00:06:04.640
Can you hear me?

00:06:04.640 --> 00:06:06.800
What'd you come to this planet for?

00:06:06.800 --> 00:06:08.110
Alien-san!

00:06:08.110 --> 00:06:10.140
Please respond!

00:06:14.670 --> 00:06:16.730
A-An alien?

00:06:15.660 --> 00:06:16.730
What's up with the wind?

00:06:17.010 --> 00:06:17.990
It looked this way!

00:06:17.990 --> 00:06:19.190
Don't look into its eyes.

00:06:19.190 --> 00:06:21.130
I'm scared of the alien...

00:06:26.380 --> 00:06:28.470
Out, Bird!

00:06:28.930 --> 00:06:30.410
So cute!

00:06:30.410 --> 00:06:31.410
Oh, wow!

00:06:31.410 --> 00:06:33.050
She hugged the alien!

00:06:33.050 --> 00:06:34.400
Oh, it's her.

00:06:34.400 --> 00:06:36.340
Huh? You know her, Pai-pai?

00:06:36.340 --> 00:06:37.660
Don't call me that!

00:06:39.170 --> 00:06:41.340
You're really so cute.

00:06:41.340 --> 00:06:42.800
Oh, it's her.

00:06:42.800 --> 00:06:44.750
What? You know her, too?

00:06:45.060 --> 00:06:45.780
Huh?

00:06:45.780 --> 00:06:46.460
What?

00:06:47.130 --> 00:06:49.340
A delicate ray of light

00:06:49.930 --> 00:06:51.710
falls upon a land illuminated by fireworks

00:06:51.710 --> 00:06:54.300
near the North Sea...

00:06:56.200 --> 00:06:58.250
Even JJ's losing his edge.

00:06:58.250 --> 00:07:02.240
But this "delicate light" 
business makes you worry.

00:07:02.240 --> 00:07:05.380
JJ's prophecies are more 
for reference than anything else.

00:07:05.380 --> 00:07:07.420
How we choose to interpret and act on them

00:07:07.420 --> 00:07:09.680
rests solely on us Gatchaman.

00:07:09.680 --> 00:07:13.350
Wow! You're really starting 
to sound like a leader.

00:07:13.350 --> 00:07:14.490
Doesn't he, Katze-san?

00:07:14.750 --> 00:07:17.300
Eh, he's just a panda!

00:07:17.840 --> 00:07:19.750
Don't call me a panda, you pyromaniac!

00:07:20.110 --> 00:07:22.040
It's coming this way.

00:07:22.040 --> 00:07:23.520
I'm scared.

00:07:23.520 --> 00:07:24.770
You don't need to be scared.

00:07:24.770 --> 00:07:27.040
She's not dangerous.

00:07:29.790 --> 00:07:31.060
Are you sure?

00:07:31.500 --> 00:07:32.220
Mom!

00:07:32.220 --> 00:07:33.210
It's only a little girl!

00:07:38.680 --> 00:07:40.260
Good morning!

00:07:40.260 --> 00:07:41.810
My name is Gelsadra!

00:07:41.810 --> 00:07:43.080
Oh, wow!

00:07:43.080 --> 00:07:44.490
It turned into a human!

00:07:44.490 --> 00:07:45.560
I'm Hajime!

00:07:45.560 --> 00:07:47.110
Nice to meet you!

00:07:47.960 --> 00:07:50.000
Gel-chan, why did you come here?

00:07:50.000 --> 00:07:51.410
Shh! Don't ask.

00:08:01.240 --> 00:08:03.150
What's this wind?

00:08:04.750 --> 00:08:05.920
Huh? What's this?

00:08:06.310 --> 00:08:08.670
Gel-chan, what's this?

00:08:08.670 --> 00:08:11.090
They're everyone's thoughts.

00:08:11.450 --> 00:08:13.360
Something weird's floating there.

00:08:11.790 --> 00:08:13.920
Mom, it's all floppy.

00:08:12.940 --> 00:08:15.010
Where'd this come from?

00:08:13.920 --> 00:08:15.710
What's this? Put it back.

00:08:15.710 --> 00:08:17.730
How strange...

00:08:16.330 --> 00:08:17.730
I'm gloomy...

00:08:20.750 --> 00:08:21.900
Wow.

00:08:21.900 --> 00:08:24.580
Everyone's so different. It's pretty.

00:08:24.580 --> 00:08:26.020
Hajime-chan, you're amazing!

00:08:26.210 --> 00:08:27.970
Amnesia, Remind!

00:08:30.420 --> 00:08:31.460
What's that?

00:08:32.260 --> 00:08:33.610
So pretty!

00:08:33.610 --> 00:08:35.640
Rock, paper, scissors!

00:08:35.640 --> 00:08:37.710
Look that way!

00:08:38.240 --> 00:08:40.350
Rock, paper, scissors!

00:08:40.790 --> 00:08:43.020
Look that way!

00:08:45.770 --> 00:08:47.840
Gel-chan's cute.

00:08:46.980 --> 00:08:49.230
She seems nice enough.

00:08:49.230 --> 00:08:51.300
That's what I thought from the start!

00:08:51.300 --> 00:08:52.150
Right!

00:08:52.150 --> 00:08:54.960
Alien-san, are you here to sightsee today?

00:08:57.670 --> 00:08:59.640
What'd you do, Gel-chan?

00:09:00.080 --> 00:09:02.890
The atmosphere just got a lot better.

00:09:03.150 --> 00:09:04.250
The atmosphere?

00:09:04.250 --> 00:09:04.890
Huh?

00:09:05.210 --> 00:09:07.720
Oh, um, the atmosphere...

00:09:07.720 --> 00:09:08.610
Tsubasa!

00:09:08.610 --> 00:09:09.540
Huh?

00:09:10.290 --> 00:09:12.020
Oh, Gel-chan.

00:09:12.020 --> 00:09:13.800
The atmosphere is...

00:09:13.800 --> 00:09:15.360
It's on this planet,

00:09:15.360 --> 00:09:16.980
and... well...

00:09:18.720 --> 00:09:19.810
Anyway!

00:09:19.810 --> 00:09:22.630
It was really fun when 
everyone came together, right?

00:09:22.630 --> 00:09:24.760
That's called a good atmosphere.

00:09:24.760 --> 00:09:26.760
Yeah, see?

00:09:26.760 --> 00:09:28.280
Good atmosphere!

00:09:33.360 --> 00:09:35.110
Thank you, Tsubasa-chan.

00:09:35.110 --> 00:09:36.560
You're welcome!

00:09:37.490 --> 00:09:39.350
Welcome to Nagaoka.

00:09:43.890 --> 00:09:45.930
So the rumors were true.

00:09:45.930 --> 00:09:47.390
I'm gloomy.

00:09:48.370 --> 00:09:49.170
Huh?

00:09:49.170 --> 00:09:51.270
Mine doesn't change.

00:09:51.270 --> 00:09:53.640
Of course yours wouldn't, Hajime-tan.

00:09:53.640 --> 00:09:54.840
Why not?

00:09:54.840 --> 00:09:57.610
Because you're you, Hajime-tan.

00:09:57.730 --> 00:10:01.370
More importantly, just let me outta 
here already, you shitty bitch!

00:10:01.370 --> 00:10:03.530
Katze-san, shut up.

00:10:06.110 --> 00:10:07.320
Late last night,

00:10:06.340 --> 00:10:09.560
I have to say, I thought I was a real goner.

00:10:07.320 --> 00:10:13.040
Prime Minister Sugayama's flight was 
attacked by several red CROWDS.

00:10:08.940 --> 00:10:12.710
<b>Even the Prime Minister Targeted!

00:10:09.560 --> 00:10:13.040
They use CROWDS, even though 
they say they're anti-CROWDS.

00:10:13.630 --> 00:10:16.790
I wonder what their goal is.

00:10:13.630 --> 00:10:16.790
The mysterious group behind the attack 
has identified itself as VAPE.

00:10:16.790 --> 00:10:19.740
There have also been reports that JSDF 
fighters were lost during the altercation,

00:10:17.280 --> 00:10:20.170
<b>I'm counting on you guys!!! 
Please vote for Mayor Shimizu!!</b>

00:10:19.280 --> 00:10:20.180
<b>It'll be the first smartphone election in history!</b>

00:10:19.740 --> 00:10:21.480
and we are seeking confirmation.

00:10:20.500 --> 00:10:25.850
It's said that "VAPE" refers to "Violent Ape." 
Aggressive monkeys, more or less.

00:10:26.330 --> 00:10:27.220
Monkeys?

00:10:27.220 --> 00:10:30.470
X, what does everyone think about CROWDS?

00:10:33.860 --> 00:10:37.900
<b>Status quo is fine (52%)
Should regulate (20%)
Should eradicate (18%)</b>

00:10:33.860 --> 00:10:37.900
Over the past week, those in favor 
of the status quo fell 12 percent.

00:10:38.120 --> 00:10:40.970
So now almost a half are revolutionaries.

00:10:40.970 --> 00:10:44.040
I'm sure the earlier incident 
from the day is a factor,

00:10:44.040 --> 00:10:46.740
but talk about a rapid 
shift in public opinion.

00:10:46.740 --> 00:10:49.920
It wasn't so long ago 
that everyone was happy

00:10:49.920 --> 00:10:52.000
saying that CROWDS changed the world...

00:10:52.460 --> 00:10:54.880
The Prime Minister's popularity 
has also gone down.

00:10:55.120 --> 00:10:57.110
Oh, man...

00:10:57.110 --> 00:11:00.700
But I'm not the sole leader of this nation.

00:11:00.700 --> 00:11:01.790
Everyone is.

00:11:01.790 --> 00:11:04.890
And CROWDS support that notion. 
They're our hope.

00:11:04.890 --> 00:11:06.600
I believe in you all.

00:11:08.340 --> 00:11:09.300
But, Prime Minister.

00:11:09.790 --> 00:11:12.520
Not all people are the same.

00:11:12.760 --> 00:11:13.580
What?

00:11:13.580 --> 00:11:15.330
Because there are some monkeys among us,

00:11:15.330 --> 00:11:18.830
this nation hasn't been able 
to produce a civilized society.

00:11:18.830 --> 00:11:21.200
That's harsh.

00:11:21.200 --> 00:11:22.530
That's reality.

00:11:23.230 --> 00:11:26.720
Our role is to grasp 
reality with objectivity

00:11:26.720 --> 00:11:28.650
and move people to action.

00:11:28.650 --> 00:11:29.810
I see.

00:11:29.810 --> 00:11:33.830
I guess becoming secretary 
to the mayor has changed what you say.

00:11:34.260 --> 00:11:36.510
No, nothing's changed.

00:11:36.880 --> 00:11:39.290
My dream has always been, and always will be,

00:11:41.500 --> 00:11:43.220
world peace.

00:11:43.480 --> 00:11:45.090
That's the spirit!

00:11:45.090 --> 00:11:48.170
Oh, The Millione Show is starting.

00:11:48.020 --> 00:11:49.010
Hello!

00:11:48.170 --> 00:11:50.930
OD's into it like usual.

00:11:49.010 --> 00:11:50.930
Happy New Year!

00:11:50.930 --> 00:11:54.860
<b>The Millione Show</b>

00:11:50.930 --> 00:11:54.860
<b>Gatchaman</b>

00:11:51.290 --> 00:11:54.860
Hello! How is everyone?

00:11:56.660 --> 00:11:57.620
Good morning.

00:11:59.850 --> 00:12:01.260
Sugane-kun!

00:12:01.950 --> 00:12:03.520
I'll sit next to him!

00:12:03.520 --> 00:12:04.590
Hey! Me first!

00:12:04.590 --> 00:12:05.730
Me, me!

00:12:04.970 --> 00:12:06.590
Please don't fight.

00:12:06.590 --> 00:12:07.960
Okay!

00:12:12.340 --> 00:12:16.670
Look at you, all happy and 
gorgeous like usual, OD!

00:12:17.030 --> 00:12:18.800
Aw, thanks.

00:12:19.270 --> 00:12:21.050
Sugane-kun, you're so cute!

00:12:21.050 --> 00:12:22.300
Please smile one more time!

00:12:23.050 --> 00:12:24.460
Oh, jeez...

00:12:23.050 --> 00:12:24.460
{Eyecatch}

00:12:32.480 --> 00:12:34.440
Don't be so small-minded! Be a man!

00:12:32.500 --> 00:12:33.970
<b>Small-Minded Celebrities!</b>

00:12:32.500 --> 00:12:33.970
<b>Even *that* celeb hottie!? 
Top 5 Closet Small-Minded Male Celebrities</b>

00:12:32.630 --> 00:12:34.440
D-san!

00:12:34.440 --> 00:12:37.020
Good job today!

00:12:35.790 --> 00:12:38.140
Tough love from you as usual, OD!

00:12:37.360 --> 00:12:38.980
Oh, it's Millio!

00:12:38.980 --> 00:12:40.820
Millio's fun.

00:12:40.820 --> 00:12:42.310
Here comes the fairy!

00:12:42.310 --> 00:12:44.190
Gross, gross, gross!

00:12:44.190 --> 00:12:46.480
OD's quite the celebrity now.

00:12:48.010 --> 00:12:49.790
Pai-pai, you're eating too much.

00:12:49.790 --> 00:12:52.540
I heard D-san's got 
three TV commercial deals.

00:12:52.980 --> 00:12:54.280
I'm gloomy.

00:12:54.640 --> 00:12:55.500
Yeesh.

00:12:56.920 --> 00:12:59.370
Oh, come to think of it, I hear 
there's someone around here

00:12:59.370 --> 00:13:01.630
who's supposed to become a new Gatchaman.

00:13:01.630 --> 00:13:04.190
Oh, really? Here in Nagaoka?

00:13:07.480 --> 00:13:09.530
A delicate ray of light

00:13:10.030 --> 00:13:11.760
falls upon a land illuminated by fireworks

00:13:11.760 --> 00:13:14.230
near the North Sea

00:13:14.920 --> 00:13:18.280
where it will meet wings 
that are still blue...

00:13:18.790 --> 00:13:20.770
What's your dream, Tsubasa-chan?

00:13:22.100 --> 00:13:23.940
Huh? Me?

00:13:23.940 --> 00:13:25.150
Well...

00:13:26.970 --> 00:13:28.700
that's to become a fireworks craftsman.

00:13:30.070 --> 00:13:31.590
Right, Yuru-jii?

00:13:33.690 --> 00:13:35.270
A fireworks craftsman, huh?

00:13:35.270 --> 00:13:36.710
That's great.

00:13:36.710 --> 00:13:40.090
Yuru-jii is a super famous 
fireworks craftsman.

00:13:40.360 --> 00:13:42.820
He's even had a movie character based on him.

00:13:43.500 --> 00:13:47.340
He made this giant Niagara fireworks, too.

00:13:47.650 --> 00:13:48.770
Wow!

00:13:48.770 --> 00:13:50.350
It's super gorgeous!

00:13:50.350 --> 00:13:55.230
Yuru-jii is basically a god here 
in Nagaoka, the fireworks capital.

00:13:55.470 --> 00:13:56.640
Don't exaggerate.

00:13:56.670 --> 00:14:06.770
<b>Nagaoka Fireworks Festival   8/2-3 2016</b>

00:13:57.030 --> 00:14:00.160
The fireworks festival is on 
the second and third of August!

00:14:00.160 --> 00:14:02.640
You should all come see it!

00:14:03.040 --> 00:14:06.780
This year's really special because 
Yuru-jii's going to be a hundred years old!

00:14:06.780 --> 00:14:08.850
A... A hundred years old?!

00:14:08.850 --> 00:14:10.140
Wow.

00:14:10.140 --> 00:14:12.310
I want to live that long, too.

00:14:14.090 --> 00:14:16.290
A hundred? That's young.

00:14:16.290 --> 00:14:18.500
Yuru-jii, do you play shogi?

00:14:18.500 --> 00:14:20.510
Don't bother, it's boring to watch.

00:14:20.510 --> 00:14:22.590
He never makes any moves.

00:14:22.590 --> 00:14:25.950
It stays just like that for weeks.

00:14:27.760 --> 00:14:29.930
I like things like that!

00:14:29.930 --> 00:14:31.200
Hey, Yuru-jii.

00:14:31.200 --> 00:14:34.050
Don't you think it's time 
you teach me about fireworks?

00:14:34.500 --> 00:14:36.610
Summer break just started today.

00:14:36.610 --> 00:14:38.230
I can't leave the business to you.

00:14:40.450 --> 00:14:42.150
That's mean. Why?

00:14:42.150 --> 00:14:43.860
What am I missing?

00:14:45.980 --> 00:14:47.490
That doesn't tell me anything!

00:14:55.280 --> 00:14:57.910
But I think you'll make it.

00:14:57.910 --> 00:14:58.660
What?

00:14:59.170 --> 00:15:02.310
I want to cheer you on, Tsubasa-chan.

00:15:02.720 --> 00:15:03.920
Gel-chan.

00:15:04.640 --> 00:15:08.840
Having a dream is a wonderful thing.

00:15:08.840 --> 00:15:10.320
Gel-chan,

00:15:11.080 --> 00:15:12.470
you're so nice!

00:15:18.650 --> 00:15:21.040
I'm cheering you on, too.

00:15:21.040 --> 00:15:23.940
I don't want to let 
this family tradition die out.

00:15:23.940 --> 00:15:26.900
Well, it's only if Yuru-jii will allow it.

00:15:26.900 --> 00:15:28.140
Just look at this footage!

00:15:28.140 --> 00:15:30.830
We're all tired to death of seeing 
them day in and day out...

00:15:30.520 --> 00:15:33.120
It's nice to have hopes 
and dreams as young'uns.

00:15:30.830 --> 00:15:32.680
but it's the red CROWDS again!

00:15:32.680 --> 00:15:34.910
Just what do they even what?

00:15:33.120 --> 00:15:35.520
But just look at the world.

00:15:34.910 --> 00:15:35.780
They're terrifying!

00:15:35.970 --> 00:15:38.760
The mysterious organization known as VAPE

00:15:38.310 --> 00:15:44.200
<b>Cowardly Terrorists</b>

00:15:38.310 --> 00:15:44.200
<b>Cut it out! 
Red CROWDS on rampage again!</b>

00:15:38.310 --> 00:15:44.200
<b>What Does the Violent CROWDS Group, VAPE, Want!?</b>

00:15:38.760 --> 00:15:42.410
is shaking the very 
foundations of this nation!

00:15:42.410 --> 00:15:46.470
Even the Prime Minister's life was in peril! 
Who is their next target?

00:15:46.470 --> 00:15:48.470
How long must we spend sleepless nights?

00:15:48.470 --> 00:15:49.970
This is unconscionable!

00:15:49.700 --> 00:15:52.680
Jeez, what are they doing?

00:15:49.970 --> 00:15:54.660
There were elderly and children 
running away in that footage!

00:15:53.120 --> 00:15:55.940
This planet still needs to be under 
protective observation for sure.

00:15:54.660 --> 00:15:55.510
Right, right.

00:15:55.510 --> 00:15:56.940
This is the act of cowards!

00:15:56.940 --> 00:16:00.110
I can't believe they'd use 
the CROWDS from far away

00:16:00.110 --> 00:16:01.690
What's wrong, Gel-chan?

00:16:00.110 --> 00:16:02.800
to attack the weak and vulnerable!

00:16:02.190 --> 00:16:04.380
I don't want this.

00:16:02.800 --> 00:16:04.220
That's right.

00:16:04.220 --> 00:16:06.320
You have a young child yourself, right?

00:16:04.380 --> 00:16:05.190
What?

00:16:05.500 --> 00:16:07.140
Everyone's all over the place.

00:16:06.320 --> 00:16:07.140
Yes, I do.

00:16:07.140 --> 00:16:08.570
That makes me sad.

00:16:07.140 --> 00:16:09.080
He's really scared.

00:16:08.570 --> 00:16:10.520
I want everyone to be united.

00:16:09.080 --> 00:16:11.950
I walk him to school and back every day now.

00:16:11.950 --> 00:16:13.830
Are all parents doing that?

00:16:13.830 --> 00:16:17.490
Of course. That's what I hear.

00:16:16.200 --> 00:16:17.490
Right?

00:16:17.490 --> 00:16:18.420
I see.

00:16:18.420 --> 00:16:19.930
Right.

00:16:20.480 --> 00:16:22.770
Gel-chan, you're so nice!

00:16:22.770 --> 00:16:24.000
You're like an angel!

00:16:24.000 --> 00:16:25.230
Did you hear that, guys?

00:16:25.230 --> 00:16:27.990
She wants everyone to be united!

00:16:27.990 --> 00:16:29.510
That's so impressive!

00:16:39.670 --> 00:16:42.610
Yuru-jii, who's that?

00:16:44.220 --> 00:16:45.420
My younger brother.

00:16:45.420 --> 00:16:47.270
I see.

00:16:47.270 --> 00:16:51.000
Jeez! Vape or Dape, I don't care!

00:16:51.000 --> 00:16:53.460
They just need to cut it out!

00:16:53.460 --> 00:16:55.790
Millio-chan, don't get too hotheaded.

00:16:55.790 --> 00:16:58.370
Give us some cheerful news once in a while!

00:16:58.700 --> 00:17:00.340
Leave that to me!

00:17:00.340 --> 00:17:02.630
Let's have a change of pace

00:17:02.630 --> 00:17:04.840
and hear a surprising piece of news!

00:17:04.840 --> 00:17:06.170
Saitou-san!

00:17:06.170 --> 00:17:09.960
<b>Emergency 
Live Broadcast!</b>

00:17:06.170 --> 00:17:09.960
<b>An Alien Invasion in Nagaoka City, Niigata Prefecture?!</b>

00:17:06.480 --> 00:17:09.010
Hi, this is Saitou from Smiling TV.

00:17:09.010 --> 00:17:12.830
A UFO just landed nearby, 
and the whole area is in an uproar.

00:17:09.140 --> 00:17:09.960
Huh?

00:17:09.960 --> 00:17:12.070
I've seen this house somewhere before.

00:17:12.070 --> 00:17:13.590
This is your home, Tsubasa!

00:17:12.830 --> 00:17:14.810
We have not only members of the press,

00:17:13.590 --> 00:17:15.400
See? Takeshi's on TV, too!

00:17:14.810 --> 00:17:16.970
but local residents gathered 
here in the hopes of

00:17:15.910 --> 00:17:17.180
What?!

00:17:16.970 --> 00:17:18.430
getting a glimpse of the UFO!

00:17:18.430 --> 00:17:21.560
This is the local home thought 
to be concealing the alien.

00:17:21.560 --> 00:17:23.420
Hello? I'm with The Millione Show!

00:17:23.420 --> 00:17:25.550
I heard there was an alien here!

00:17:30.350 --> 00:17:31.610
Oh! Paiman-san!

00:17:32.000 --> 00:17:34.230
Wait. Does this mean there is an alien here?

00:17:34.780 --> 00:17:38.750
We have, indeed, placed an extraterrestrial 
life form under our protective custody.

00:17:38.750 --> 00:17:39.930
Really?!

00:17:39.930 --> 00:17:41.160
Calm down!

00:17:41.160 --> 00:17:43.330
She is not dangerous.

00:17:43.350 --> 00:17:48.200
<b>Emergency 
Live Broadcast!</b>

00:17:43.350 --> 00:17:48.200
<b>An Alien Invasion in Nagaoka City, Niigata Prefecture?!</b>

00:17:43.880 --> 00:17:48.210
She could even be a savior 
who's come to help this planet!

00:17:48.440 --> 00:17:49.860
A savior?!

00:17:49.860 --> 00:17:53.880
Will world peace finally be achieved, OD?

00:17:54.140 --> 00:17:56.340
Oh, how fun!

00:17:56.340 --> 00:17:58.920
This planet's been way too dangerous lately!

00:17:58.920 --> 00:18:01.140
Oh, Utsutsu!

00:18:02.750 --> 00:18:06.060
We'll release an official statement 
on Gatchannel in the near future.

00:18:06.300 --> 00:18:10.360
Do leave the citizens alone until then.

00:18:11.950 --> 00:18:13.570
Oh, it's Tsubasa-chan!

00:18:13.570 --> 00:18:14.720
Do you have a comment?

00:18:13.570 --> 00:18:14.720
You're Tsubasa-chan?

00:18:14.720 --> 00:18:16.490
The camera, quick!

00:18:17.390 --> 00:18:18.250
Hey!

00:18:19.870 --> 00:18:20.970
You idiot!

00:18:20.970 --> 00:18:22.660
What are you thinking?!

00:18:28.940 --> 00:18:30.880
Who are you, Mister?

00:18:33.320 --> 00:18:34.470
JJ!

00:18:34.470 --> 00:18:35.790
This means...

00:18:35.790 --> 00:18:36.720
I'm gloomy.

00:18:36.720 --> 00:18:38.480
Hey, are you recording this?

00:18:38.480 --> 00:18:39.640
Yes...

00:18:39.640 --> 00:18:40.550
Tsubasa.

00:18:41.110 --> 00:18:45.520
Everyone has power that 
is concealed deep within.

00:18:46.170 --> 00:18:48.870
Only those who realize that 
they possess this power

00:18:49.310 --> 00:18:51.670
will awaken to their greater purpose.

00:18:53.330 --> 00:18:54.650
Awaken!

00:18:56.960 --> 00:19:00.320
Spread your as-of-yet 
invisible wings...

00:19:12.900 --> 00:19:14.340
Thy name is...

00:19:14.680 --> 00:19:16.110
Gatchaman!

00:19:17.470 --> 00:19:18.960
G-Gatchaman?!

00:19:18.960 --> 00:19:20.020
Me?!

00:19:22.690 --> 00:19:24.720
Ow...

00:19:26.940 --> 00:19:27.960
Whoa!

00:19:27.960 --> 00:19:28.990
What's this?!

00:19:28.990 --> 00:19:32.340
Hmm, those wings are still blue, all right.

00:19:32.340 --> 00:19:34.190
This is a huge scoop!

00:19:34.190 --> 00:19:35.430
What's your name?

00:19:35.430 --> 00:19:37.210
How do you feel about being 
chosen to be a Gatchaman?!

00:19:37.210 --> 00:19:38.840
Huh? Well...

00:19:38.840 --> 00:19:40.020
Try to transform for us!

00:19:40.300 --> 00:19:41.660
Huh? Transform?

00:19:42.050 --> 00:19:42.740
Camera?!

00:19:42.740 --> 00:19:43.490
Ready!

00:19:43.880 --> 00:19:46.780
Go, Bird!

00:19:47.650 --> 00:19:48.490
Huh?

00:19:49.390 --> 00:19:52.100
Go, Bird?

00:19:52.650 --> 00:19:53.830
Why?!

00:19:53.830 --> 00:19:54.760
Do you have a boyfriend?

00:19:54.760 --> 00:19:55.930
Who do you look up to?

00:19:55.930 --> 00:19:57.340
Who's your favorite Gatchaman?

00:19:57.340 --> 00:19:58.590
How old are you?

00:19:58.590 --> 00:19:59.720
Hey, don't—

00:19:58.590 --> 00:19:59.720
Do you have a boyfriend?

00:19:59.720 --> 00:20:00.640
Are you a high school student?

00:20:00.640 --> 00:20:02.380
Don't talk all at once!

00:20:04.470 --> 00:20:05.970
Cut it...

00:20:05.970 --> 00:20:07.830
out!

00:20:10.240 --> 00:20:12.730
It's a new Gatchaman...

00:20:19.780 --> 00:20:21.040
How do you feel?

00:20:23.450 --> 00:20:24.980
Get out, now!

00:20:24.980 --> 00:20:26.360
I'll deck you!

00:20:26.360 --> 00:20:27.330
Deck?

00:20:27.330 --> 00:20:30.140
She's saying she'll beat you all up.

00:20:30.140 --> 00:20:31.080
What?!

00:20:33.350 --> 00:20:34.300
Huh?!

00:20:34.300 --> 00:20:35.500
I transformed?

00:20:35.500 --> 00:20:36.590
How?

00:20:37.240 --> 00:20:38.420
Oh, yeah!

00:20:41.760 --> 00:20:45.090
The air here is great!

00:20:48.950 --> 00:20:50.090
Exhale properly.

00:20:50.910 --> 00:20:52.810
Huh? A new Gatchaman!

00:20:53.450 --> 00:20:54.650
Another girl...

00:20:54.650 --> 00:20:56.920
This is a tremendous scoop!

00:20:54.650 --> 00:21:03.400
<b>A New Gatchaman Is Born!</b>

00:20:56.920 --> 00:20:59.360
OD, do give us the lowdown later!

00:20:59.940 --> 00:21:03.400
Who cares about those barbaric VAPE people!

00:21:04.360 --> 00:21:08.440
This planet is still 
the planet of the apes...

00:21:16.540 --> 00:21:19.880
<b>The First Smart Phone Elections in History!
Tachikawa City Mayoral Elections</b>

00:21:16.540 --> 00:21:19.880
<b>Vote with Your Thumb</b>

00:21:16.780 --> 00:21:17.780
Huh?

00:21:17.780 --> 00:21:19.380
Voting in the elections 
using your smartphone?

00:21:19.880 --> 00:21:20.820
Yeah.

00:21:20.820 --> 00:21:23.130
You can vote once you're sixteen.

00:21:23.130 --> 00:21:25.180
Then we can, too?

00:21:25.720 --> 00:21:30.600
Yeah, I hear the next Prime Minister will 
be chosen through smart phone votes, too.

00:21:30.600 --> 00:21:32.060
Isn't that amazing?

00:21:32.060 --> 00:21:33.090
Seriously?

00:21:33.090 --> 00:21:35.290
Kae-chan, isn't that too "easy"?

00:21:35.890 --> 00:21:38.440
Well, that's the world we live in.

00:21:38.440 --> 00:21:40.390
Who are you trying to be?

00:21:40.390 --> 00:21:42.030
Those are the times we live in.

00:21:40.390 --> 00:21:42.030
{ED}
